/// One attempt by an agent to publish, and how it ended. A row exists before
/// anything reaches X, so a post here is the attempt and its outcome rather than
/// only the text that went out.
///
/// The row is written unresolved before the X call and resolved after it. That
/// ordering is what makes an attempt at most once: X publishes no idempotency key
/// for creating a post, so a row left unresolved by a crash is never picked up
/// again and the slot behind it is gone.
///
/// Nothing deletes a row. X obliges an app to delete content within 24 hours of a
/// request and everything within ten business days if API access ends. AI Launchpad
/// keeps its rows regardless, and that is a decision rather than an oversight.
model Post {
  /// Row identity, because one token holds many of these. A version 7 UUID, which
  /// is ordered by creation time, so new rows append to the index rather than
  /// landing at random through it.
  id String @id @default(uuid(7))

  /// The token whose agent wrote it, always lowercased, as the agents table
  /// already is. Indexed and never unique: many rows for one token is the point.
  token String

  /// What the agent wrote. Kept whatever the outcome, because a row that failed is
  /// the only record of what was nearly published in the creator's name.
  text String

  /// Where the attempt stands. A row that reached X is born unresolved and moves
  /// once, to published or to failed, and never back. A row that was never sent is
  /// born dry and never moves at all.
  outcome PostOutcome

  /// Why a failed row failed. Null on every other outcome.
  reason String?

  /// The post's identifier at X, set once on success. It and the publish log are
  /// the only handle an admin has on what an agent actually said.
  xPostId String?

  /// What X charged and what the model charged, as charged at the time rather than
  /// as a constant read back at query time. X already changed its pricing once this
  /// year, and a constant in code would silently rewrite the cost of every post
  /// made before the change.
  ///
  /// Scale is eight places because a post costs around $0.0004 and a scale of two
  /// records every one of them as zero. Both sit at zero until something is
  /// charged, so an attempt that never reached X carries no figure it did not incur.
  xCost      Decimal @default(0) @db.Decimal(18, 8)
  writerCost Decimal @default(0) @db.Decimal(18, 8)

  /// What the writer consumed and produced. They sit beside the money because a
  /// derived figure with nothing behind it cannot be checked when a bill looks
  /// wrong.
  inputTokens  Int @default(0)
  outputTokens Int @default(0)

  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  /// Serves the read of what a token's agent already said, published or dry, which
  /// orders by createdAt descending.
  @@index([token, createdAt])
  @@map("posts")
}

/// How an attempt ended. Unresolved is the state a row is born in, and the state a
/// crash between the write and X's answer leaves behind for good.
///
/// Dry is the one outcome a row is born in rather than moved to. X was never
/// called, so there is no answer to wait for and nothing to resolve, and it is
/// never counted among the rows the cost of the product is read from.
enum PostOutcome {
  unresolved
  published
  failed
  dry
}
